{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtapositionMonoid","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtapositionMonoid","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.FreeMonoid.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.TypeTags.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Equiv.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Sigma.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":55,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.tuple_free_blocks_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.tuple_free_blocks_commute","kind":"theorem","line":491,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L491-L496","doc":"… and yet the images of the two block inclusions still commute there. Together with\n`tuple_free_noncommutative` this is the precise sense in which `juxLeft_commute_juxRight` is a\nstatement about the *blocks*, not an artefact of a commutative witness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.tuple_free_noncommutative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.tuple_free_noncommutative","kind":"theorem","line":485,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L485-L489","doc":"**The commutation theorem is not vacuously true.** Over `FreeMonoid Bool` the ambient tuple\nmonoid on `1 + 1` strands genuinely fails to be commutative … ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.freeMonoidBool_noncommutative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.freeMonoidBool_noncommutative","kind":"theorem","line":478,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L478-L483","doc":"A concrete noncommutative monoid, so that `tuple_noncommutative` has an actual witness and is\nnot left conditional on an unmet hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.tuple_noncommutative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.tuple_noncommutative","kind":"theorem","line":472,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L472-L476","doc":"**The tuple fibres are noncommutative when `M` is.** So in this model the ambient monoid in\nwhich `juxLeft_commute_juxRight` asserts a commutation is itself not commutative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.instJuxtaposableMonoidTuple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.instJuxtaposableMonoidTuple","kind":"instance","line":458,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L458-L470","doc":"**The tuple model satisfies the interchange law over an arbitrary monoid** — commutativity of\nthe fibre is *not* required, because the two blocks occupy disjoint coordinates. Contrast\n`instJuxtaposableMonoidConst`, where `jux` *is* the multiplication and therefore, by\n`const_interchange_iff_commutative`, the fibre is forced to commute. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.tuple_jux_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.tuple_jux_right","kind":"theorem","line":454,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L454-L456","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.tuple_jux_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.tuple_jux_left","kind":"theorem","line":450,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L450-L452","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.instJuxtaposableTuple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.instJuxtaposableTuple","kind":"instance","line":440,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L440-L448","doc":"**Concatenation of tuples is a juxtaposition.** The three laws are `Fin.append_assoc`,\n`Fin.elim0_append` and `Fin.append_elim0`; only the first two need the index transport, since\n`n + 0` reduces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.TupleFamily","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.TupleFamily","kind":"def","line":429,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L429-L431","doc":"Tuples of length `n` in a monoid `M`, multiplied pointwise (`Pi.monoid`). Like `WordFamily`\nthis really depends on the index; unlike `Const M` its fibres need not be commutative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.wordEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.wordEquiv","kind":"def","line":412,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L412-L417","doc":"**The juxtaposition monoid of the word model is the free monoid.** This pins the abstract\nconstruction down completely on a dependent family: `Σ n, WordFamily α n` under side-by-side union\nis `FreeMonoid α`, on the nose. In particular the juxtaposition monoid is in general\nnoncommutative and infinite, so `Juxtaposable` is very far from vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.wordTotal_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.wordTotal_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":409,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L409-L410","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.wordTotal_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.wordTotal_injective","kind":"theorem","line":403,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L403-L407","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.wordTotal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.wordTotal","kind":"def","line":398,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L398-L401","doc":"Reading off the underlying word is a monoid hom from the word model's juxtaposition monoid to\nthe free monoid on `α`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.word_jux_val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.word_jux_val","kind":"theorem","line":387,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L387-L389","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.instJuxtaposableWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.instJuxtaposableWord","kind":"instance","line":377,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L377-L385","doc":"**Concatenation makes words juxtaposable.** The two sigma-level laws are `List.append_assoc`\nand `List.nil_append` transported by `Sigma.subtype_ext`; the right-unit law is `List.append_nil`\nwith no transport at all, because `n + 0` reduces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.WordFamily","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.WordFamily","kind":"def","line":373,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L373-L375","doc":"Words of length `n` in an alphabet `α`. Unlike `Const`, this family really depends on the\nindex, so it exercises the casts in `jux_assoc` and `empty_jux`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.writhe_strandCount_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.writhe_strandCount_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":361,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L361-L364","doc":"Every strand count is realised in the writhe model. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.writheTotal_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.writheTotal_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":356,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L356-L359","doc":"**The writhe model is non-degenerate**: its juxtaposition monoid surjects onto `ℤ`, so the\nmodel is very far from a one-point family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.writheTotal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.writheTotal","kind":"def","line":352,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L352-L354","doc":"Total writhe of a juxtaposed system, as a monoid hom out of the juxtaposition monoid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.WritheFamily","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.WritheFamily","kind":"def","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L347-L350","doc":"The **writhe model**: every strand count carries `ℤ` written multiplicatively, and juxtaposition\nadds writhes. This is the abelianisation picture — the exponent sum of a braid word is additive\nunder disjoint union — and it is a faithful model of `JuxtaposableMonoid`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.instJuxtaposableMonoidConst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.instJuxtaposableMonoidConst","kind":"instance","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L339-L345","doc":"The constant family on a commutative monoid satisfies the interchange law. By\n`const_interchange_iff_commutative` commutativity is not merely convenient here — it is exactly\nwhat the interchange law demands of this model. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.const_empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.const_empty","kind":"theorem","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L336-L337","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.const_jux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.const_jux","kind":"theorem","line":332,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L332-L334","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.instJuxtaposableConst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.instJuxtaposableConst","kind":"instance","line":322,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L322-L330","doc":"Any commutative monoid gives a juxtaposable constant family, with `jux` the multiplication.\nThe two sigma-level laws go through `sigma_const_eq`, since the family does not actually depend on\nthe index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.Const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.Const","kind":"def","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L312-L313","doc":"The constant family `n ↦ M`: every strand count carries the same object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.ofMultiplicative_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.ofMultiplicative_comp","kind":"theorem","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L299-L306","doc":"**`ofMultiplicative` is surjective onto the monoid homs**: every `φ : (Σ n, F n) →* M` is\n`ofMultiplicative` applied to its own restriction to the fibres. With `map_jux` this makes the\ncorrespondence between juxtaposition-multiplicative functionals and monoid homs a bijection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.map_jux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.map_jux","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L293-L297","doc":"**Conversely, every monoid hom out of the juxtaposition monoid is multiplicative under\njuxtaposition.** Together with `ofMultiplicative_comp` this says the two notions coincide. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.ofMultiplicative_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.ofMultiplicative_apply","kind":"theorem","line":287,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L287-L291","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.ofMultiplicative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.ofMultiplicative","kind":"def","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L269-L285","doc":"**A juxtaposition-multiplicative functional is a monoid hom out of the juxtaposition monoid.**\n\nGiven a family of functionals `f n : F n → M` that is normalised on the empty braid and turns\njuxtaposition into multiplication, `ofMultiplicative` assembles it into a genuine\n`(Σ n, F n) →* M`.\n\nThis is the abstract statement behind\n`QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceMultiplicative.markovTrace_juxtapose`: that file discharges the\nhypothesis `hmul` for the matrix trace on the Kronecker model of disjoint strands; this\nconstruction is what the hypothesis buys you. In particular `MonoidHom.map_pow` immediately gives\nthe value on `k` disjoint copies of one component. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.const_interchange_iff_commutative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.const_interchange_iff_commutative","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L249-L261","doc":"**The interchange law is not automatic.** For the constant family with `jux = (*)`, the\ninterchange law holds if and only if the fibre monoid is commutative. So `JuxtaposableMonoid` is a\nreal constraint: a noncommutative fibre with `jux = (*)` refutes it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.juxLeft_commute_juxRight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.juxLeft_commute_juxRight","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L240-L245","doc":"**The two blocks do not interact.** The images of the two block inclusions commute inside\n`F (m + n)`. For braid groups this is far commutation, `σᵢ σⱼ = σⱼ σᵢ` when `i` and `j` lie in\ndifferent blocks — and here it is a *consequence* of the interchange law, not an extra axiom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.jux_eq_juxRight_mul_juxLeft","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.jux_eq_juxRight_mul_juxLeft","kind":"theorem","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L234-L238","doc":"The same juxtaposition factors in the *other* order too. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.jux_eq_juxLeft_mul_juxRight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.jux_eq_juxLeft_mul_juxRight","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L228-L232","doc":"A juxtaposition factors as *left block* times *right block*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.juxRight_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.juxRight_apply","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L226-L226","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.juxLeft_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.juxLeft_apply","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L224-L224","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.juxRight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.juxRight","kind":"def","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L216-L222","doc":"The **right block inclusion** `F n →* F (m + n)`: pad on the left with `m` trivial strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.juxLeft","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.juxLeft","kind":"def","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L208-L214","doc":"The **left block inclusion** `F m →* F (m + n)`: pad on the right with `n` trivial strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.juxHom_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.juxHom_apply","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L205-L206","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.juxHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.juxHom","kind":"def","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L198-L203","doc":"**Juxtaposition is a monoid homomorphism out of the product of the two blocks.** This is the\ninterchange law repackaged; it is the precise sense in which `jux` is bifunctorial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.JuxtaposableMonoid.jux_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.JuxtaposableMonoid.jux_mul","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L191-L191","doc":"The interchange law: the two blocks compose independently. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.JuxtaposableMonoid.jux_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.JuxtaposableMonoid.jux_one","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L189-L189","doc":"Juxtaposing the two units gives the unit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.JuxtaposableMonoid.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.JuxtaposableMonoid.mk","kind":"ctor","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L187-L187","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.JuxtaposableMonoid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.JuxtaposableMonoid","kind":"class","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L176-L192","doc":"A juxtaposable family whose fibres are monoids, satisfying the **interchange law**\n\n    jux (a * a') (b * b') = jux a b * jux a' b'.\n\nThis is the algebraic statement that the two strand blocks *do not interact*: composing inside each\nblock and then juxtaposing is the same as juxtaposing and then composing. For the Artin braid\ngroups it is the assertion that `Bₘ × Bₙ → Bₘ₊ₙ` is a group homomorphism, i.e. that the image is\nthe parabolic subgroup on the two blocks.\n\nBoth fields are quantified equations in the shape of the claim; see\n`const_interchange_iff_commutative` for a proof that they are a genuine restriction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.strandCount_mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.strandCount_mk","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L170-L172","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.strandCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.strandCount","kind":"def","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L163-L168","doc":"**Juxtaposition adds strand counts**, packaged as a monoid homomorphism to the natural numbers\nunder addition. This is the grading of the juxtaposition monoid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.one_eq_empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.one_eq_empty","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L160-L161","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.mk_mul_mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.mk_mul_mk","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L156-L158","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.instMonoidSigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.instMonoidSigma","kind":"instance","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L146-L154","doc":"**The juxtaposition monoid.** The disjoint union of all strand counts, `Σ n, F n`, is a monoid\nunder side-by-side union, with the empty braid as unit. Working on the disjoint union is what makes\njuxtaposition expressible as a *homogeneous* binary operation at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.Juxtaposable.jux_empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.Juxtaposable.jux_empty","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L140-L140","doc":"The empty braid is a right unit. No cast is needed: `n + 0` reduces to `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.Juxtaposable.empty_jux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.Juxtaposable.empty_jux","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L138-L138","doc":"The empty braid is a left unit, as an equality in `Σ i, F i` (`0 + n = n` is part of the\nstatement, since `0 + n` does not reduce). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.Juxtaposable.jux_assoc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.Juxtaposable.jux_assoc","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L134-L134","doc":"Juxtaposition is associative, as an equality in `Σ i, F i` (the index equality\n`(m + n) + k = m + (n + k)` is part of the statement). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.Juxtaposable.empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.Juxtaposable.empty","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L131-L131","doc":"The empty braid, on zero strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.Juxtaposable.jux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.Juxtaposable.jux","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L129-L129","doc":"Side-by-side union of a braid on `m` strands with one on `n` strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.Juxtaposable.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.Juxtaposable.mk","kind":"ctor","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L127-L127","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.Juxtaposable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidJuxtaposition.Juxtaposable","kind":"class","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidJuxtapositionMonoid.lean#L120-L140","doc":"A **juxtaposable family**: a family of \"braid-like\" objects indexed by strand count, with a\nside-by-side union `jux : F m → F n → F (m + n)` and an empty object on `0` strands.\n\nThe three laws are associativity, and the two unit laws. Associativity and the *left* unit law are\nstated as equalities in `Σ i, F i`, because their two sides live in types indexed by\npropositionally- but not definitionally-equal naturals (`(m + n) + k` vs `m + (n + k)`, and `0 + n`\nvs `n`). The *right* unit law needs no such packaging, since `n + 0` reduces to `n`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}